<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manendragarh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manendragarh is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, in the area of the former princely state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, or Koriya. It grew with the development of the nearby coalfields and the railway in the 20th century, and since 2022 it has been the headquarters of the Manendragarh-Chirmiri-Bharatpur district.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manendragarh.jpg" alt="Manendragarh" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kailash Mohankar · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amritdhara_Waterfall_on_Hasdeo_River_in_Koriya_Distt,_Chhattisgarh_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
